    "body": "Cross-OS check of the ui suite (mkinney's machines), main at `6f8b309d`, `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --no-fail-fast` (debug, default suite, CWD `crates/ui`):\n\n| Machine | OS | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| dude | Linux x86-64 (Debian 13), headless: `xvfb-run` + Mesa software rendering | 940 passed, **2 failed**, 7 ignored |\n| m3 | macOS (Apple M3 Max) | 813 passed in the lib binary, **2 failed**, 6 ignored; all other ui binaries ok |\n\nThe same two tests fail on both systems, and only these two:\n- `detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_with_only_a_wide_hole_is_refused` (`crates/ui/src/detect_holes_note_tests.rs:108`)\n- `detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_stores_the_small_hole_and_names_the_wide_one` (`crates/ui/src/detect_holes_note_tests.rs:97`)\n\nSo the failure is not OS-specific, display-specific or flaky. It matches the cause in this issue: PR #1839 (Bore clears wide holes with rings) changed what Detect holes keeps, and the tests still expect the old refusal. No other ui test fails, so your fix PR #1912 should make the ui suite green. A Codex review of #1912 is queued on our side, so that it can merge sooner.\n\n(A note for headless Linux runners: `xvfb-run` needs the `xauth` package. Without it, xvfb-run exits before the tests start.)\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
