    "body": "Run 43723593734 at 6f8b309dc (post-merge batch gate) is red. Three tests fail in two suites. Full logs: artifact gate-logs-post-merge-43723593734-1, dir batch-20261115-141836.\n\nui suites (same two as run 43718974511):\n- detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_with_only_a_wide_hole_is_refused\n- detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_stores_the_small_hole_and_names_the_wide_one\nPR #1912 fixes these. It has a clean collaborator review marker at head 078564142 and label merge-ready.\n\napp suites (two NEW failures; the first bulk run had this suite green):\n- troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources — crates/app/tests/docs_troubleshooting.rs:83. The test reads site/content/guide/troubleshooting.md. PR #1908 (commit 89b43e04d, \"fix(docs): group the user guide by job stage\") moved that page. The path in the test is now wrong.\n- threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit — crates/app/tests/operations.rs:1433. The fixture creates an APocket3D op (pocket3d_params_5) and calls expect(\"create op\"). PR #1895 (commit 5adf0114d, \"fix(3d): refuse pocket depths beyond tool assembly reach\") adds a reach refusal. The fixture now looks refused by that law, or the batch and serial paths answer differently.\n\nDone means unchanged: one green batch run on a head that carries the fixes for all three tests.\n",
